---
import BaseLayout from "../../layouts/BaseLayout.astro";
import SiteHeader from "../../components/SiteHeader.astro";
import SiteFooter from "../../components/SiteFooter.astro";
import { Image } from "astro:assets";
import delta from "../../images/projects/australia-2024-qualifying-delta.png";
import turnThree from "../../images/projects/australia-2024-turn-3.png";
import "../../styles/projects.css";
const original = "https://github.com/Nelson-Jnrnd/nelson-jnrnd.github.io/blob/main/archive/legacy-site-2026-06-02/_posts/2024-03-23-How-Ocon-got-out-of-Q1.md";
---

<BaseLayout title="Formula 1 analysis · Nelson Jeanrenaud" description="A sample of my Python telemetry analysis: comparing Ocon and Gasly in qualifying at the 2024 Australian Grand Prix, with original archived charts.">
  <SiteHeader />
  <span id="top"></span>
  <main class="wrap project-detail">
    <section class="section">
      <a class="project-detail__back" href="/#projects">Back to projects</a>
      <p class="kicker">Personal project · Python · 2021–2024</p>
      <h1>Formula 1 data analysis</h1>
      <p class="lead">Turning race telemetry into an explanation of where lap time is gained and lost.</p>
      <p>I built Python tooling for telemetry and session analysis and published race-weekend reports. This sample revisits my article “How Ocon got out of Q1”, published on 23 March 2024.</p>
    </section>
    <section class="section" aria-labelledby="question">
      <h2 id="question">The question</h2>
      <p>At the 2024 Australian Grand Prix, Ocon reached the second qualifying session while Gasly did not. I compared their laps to investigate where the difference emerged, using time-delta and corner-level telemetry charts.</p>
      <figure class="project-evidence">
        <a href={delta.src} target="_blank" rel="noopener noreferrer" aria-label="Open the qualifying time-delta chart at full size">
          <Image src={delta} alt="Time-delta chart comparing Ocon and Gasly across a qualifying lap at the 2024 Australian Grand Prix." width={1200} />
        </a>
        <figcaption>Original time-delta chart from the archived article. Open the image for a closer look.</figcaption>
      </figure>
    </section>
    <section class="section" aria-labelledby="comparison">
      <h2 id="comparison">From lap time to driving behaviour</h2>
      <p>My turn-three analysis associated Ocon's later braking and greater corner-entry speed with a gain of about two tenths. Comparing speed, throttle and brake traces helped distinguish the drivers' approaches rather than treating the final lap time as the whole explanation.</p>
      <figure class="project-evidence">
        <a href={turnThree.src} target="_blank" rel="noopener noreferrer" aria-label="Open the turn-three telemetry chart at full size">
          <Image src={turnThree} alt="Original turn-three comparison chart showing Ocon and Gasly's telemetry and relative time difference." width={1200} loading="lazy" />
        </a>
        <figcaption>The original corner-level chart used to examine turn three.</figcaption>
      </figure>
      <h3>What the data cannot establish</h3>
      <p>Public telemetry is incomplete. Brake-pedal pressure is unavailable, and recorded gear changes do not necessarily show attempted shifts. My original article therefore left the impact of Gasly's reported shifting problems unresolved. The charts support observations of the recorded traces; they cannot recover every cause behind them.</p>
    </section>
    <section class="section" aria-labelledby="evidence">
      <h2 id="evidence">Explore the work</h2>
      <ul class="project-detail__sources">
        <li><a href={original} target="_blank" rel="noopener noreferrer">Read the original archived article</a></li>
        <li><a href="https://github.com/Nelson-Jnrnd/F1_Telemetry_Charts" target="_blank" rel="noopener noreferrer">Inspect the telemetry-chart tooling</a></li>
        <li><a href="/projects/pit-stop-modelling">Related academic work: pit-stop decision modelling</a></li>
      </ul>
    </section>
  </main>
  <SiteFooter />
</BaseLayout>
